SUMMARY:Lauren Daigle at American Music Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Lauren Daigle is a multi-GRAMMY®-winning\, chart-topping vocalist whose powerful\, soulful sound has captivated audiences around the globe. With more than a billion streams worldwide and sold-out tours spanning North America\, Europe\, Australia\, and Africa\, she has graced some of the world’s most iconic stages\, from Carnegie Hall and Red Rocks to Radio City Music Hall\, the New Orleans Jazz Fest\, and Lollapalooza. She has also performed on one of the world’s biggest stages\, singing “America the Beautiful” at the Super Bowl alongside Trombone Shorty. \nHer breakthrough album Look Up Child (2x platinum) debuted at No. 3 on the Billboard Top 200 and made history as Daigle became the first female artist to simultaneously land in the Top 10 of both the Pop and Christian album charts. The album’s 6x platinum hit single “You Say” became one of the longest-running No. 1 songs in Billboard chart history. \nDaigle’s GRAMMY®-nominated self-titled album features standout tracks including “Thank God I Do\,” “These Are the Days\,” and “Be Okay\,” and fueled her wildly successful Kaleidoscope Tour and Kaleidoscope Nights\, which played to packed arenas and was extended by popular demand. Beyond the music\, Daigle is known for her commitment to giving back through her nonprofit\, The Price Fund\, which supports organizations focused on music education\, hunger relief\, and care for the elderly—making her impact felt both on and off the stage. \n\nCome Explore Our Lancaster Theaters and the Arts\n\n\nLive Theater\nLive Entertainment\nLive Music\n\n\n\nDinner Theaters\nMurder Mysteries\nThings To Do\n\n\n\nArtisan Collectives\nArt Galleries\nEvents Calendar
